{"findings":[{"rule_id":"NM-002","evidence":[{"kind":"note","ref":"N1","page":1,"quote":"3) THREADS TO BE KEEP SOFT."},{"kind":"note","ref":"N1","page":1,"quote":"4) RETAPPING TO BE DONE AFTER SURFACE TREATMENT AT SUPPLIER END.( IF APPLICABLE )"}],"comment":"Note N1 instructs to keep threads soft (item 3) yet also requires retapping after surface treatment (item 4), which is contradictory because retapping hardened or treated threads implies they were not kept soft, and retapping soft threads after plating is unnecessary. This ambiguity can cause the supplier to either skip a required operation or damage the part; the designer should clarify whether the threads are masked during case hardening and plating so that no retapping is needed, or state the exact sequence of operations unambiguously."
    ,
    "recommended_correction": "Revise note N1 to remove the contradiction: if threads are masked before heat treatment and plating to remain soft, delete item 4; if retapping is genuinely required, explain why it does not conflict with keeping the threads soft."}]}
